# Docker reads the .dockerignore next to the *context*, and the context is
# backend/ — set by the Railway service's Root Directory. A .dockerignore at
# the repo root would be silently inert; do not add one back there.
#
# Nothing outside backend/ is in the context at all, so the repo-root .env
# cannot reach the builder even though nothing here mentions it.

.venv/
tests/

__pycache__/
*.pyc
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/

.env
.env.*

*.md
